@@ -20,6 +20,8 @@ Messages, files, profiles and the setup messages of voice connections are encryp
 
 **Friends and direct messages.** Users can send each other friend requests by username, accept them and block people. Messages from a blocked person in text rooms are collapsed and their voice is muted on your side.
 
+**Status and automatic idle.** The Online, Idle, Do Not Disturb or Invisible status and an encrypted custom status text are chosen from the avatar menu. Do not disturb mutes notifications and message sounds, and an invisible person appears offline to others. Automatic idle is on by default: if the mouse, keyboard, touch or a gamepad is not used on a device for 10 minutes, that device counts as idle. Once all of a person's open devices are idle, others see the person as Idle, the person's own status reads "Idle (automatic)", and the first input brings them back to Online. A device in a voice room never counts as idle, and the desktop app also counts use of other apps on the computer. Automatic idle only affects the Online status, never touches a status you chose yourself and is not written to disk. It can be turned off for this device in Settings > Privacy, where the time can be set to 5, 10, 15, 30 or 60 minutes. The server and members can see when a person went inactive. In the browser the timers of a background tab can be slowed down, so the decision may be up to about a minute late.
+
 **Voice chat.** Audio flows directly between people over WebRTC and does not pass through the server. You choose between voice activity detection (with an automatic or manual threshold) and push to talk. The choice can also be made from a small menu that opens when you right click the microphone button (Shift+F10 on the keyboard). A keyboard key, a mouse side button or a gamepad button can be assigned to push to talk, mute and deafen. When you join a voice room, a radio card that looks like a handheld radio opens: the people in the room, a halo around the speaker, a large Push to talk button, and buttons in two rows, each in its own color (Camera, Microphone and Deafen on top, Screen and Leave below, on phones only icons in a single row). The volume of each person can be set between 0% and 200%, and anything above 100% boosts that person's voice on the device. Because the boosted voice plays from the browser's audio context, Chromium's echo cancellation may not take it into account, so echo may reach the other side when you use speakers. Headphones avoid this. A distinct 2 second notification sound plays when someone joins or leaves the voice room, when someone starts a screen share, when a direct message or a friend request arrives and when you drop out of the voice room. The sounds are not played from files, they are synthesized on the device. Their volume is set with the slider in Settings > Notifications (40% by default), where each sound can also be played. Advanced noise suppression (RNNoise) suppresses non-speech sounds such as keyboard clicks on the device before they reach others, and it is on by default. By default up to 8 people can join a voice room, and the owner of the frequency can change this limit between 2 and 12 people in Settings > General.
 
 **Screen sharing.** Anyone in a voice room can share their screen, a window or a tab. When a share starts, it appears with a Watch button in the Notifications list of the people in the same voice room, and hovering over the person sharing in the crew of the radio card also shows a Watch stream button (always visible on touch screens). Video is sent only to people who start watching. The person sharing chooses between smooth motion and sharp text, a resolution of 720p or 1080p, and a frame rate of 15 or 30. Whether audio is shared is chosen only in the window where the source is picked (the browser's picker, or the app's own picker in the desktop app). The audio is requested with the `restrictOwnAudio` constraint, which leaves out Telsiz's own sounds: the desktop app and browsers that support it remove the conversation, notification sounds and Telsiz DJ playing in Telsiz from the shared audio. On older Windows versions that do not support this separation, all system audio is shared.
@@ -142,7 +144,7 @@ There are three ways to reach friends on the internet. The `tunel.bat` (Windows)
 
 The password is never sent to the server. The browser derives an authentication key and a separate wrapping key from the password with scrypt. Group content is encrypted with TweetNaCl-js using XSalsa20-Poly1305, and direct messages with a shared key established over X25519. The server checks authorization on every request, validates input, and applies rate limits and a strict Content Security Policy.
 
-End-to-end encryption does not hide everything. The server sees who is online, who is in which room and voice room, the timing and size of messages, room names, usernames and the typing status. If the owner has turned on search by song name, it also sees the song names searched with `/play`. In the web version the app code comes from the server, so an active attacker who takes over the server could serve modified code. The group key has no forward secrecy. In voice and video chat people can see each other's IP address. The project has not had an independent security audit. The full list of limits is in [docs/ARCHITECTURE.md](docs/ARCHITECTURE.md#limits), and the way to report a vulnerability is in [SECURITY.md](SECURITY.md).
+End-to-end encryption does not hide everything. The server sees who is online, if automatic idle is on when someone went inactive, who is in which room and voice room, the timing and size of messages, room names, usernames and the typing status. If the owner has turned on search by song name, it also sees the song names searched with `/play`. In the web version the app code comes from the server, so an active attacker who takes over the server could serve modified code. The group key has no forward secrecy. In voice and video chat people can see each other's IP address. The project has not had an independent security audit. The full list of limits is in [docs/ARCHITECTURE.md](docs/ARCHITECTURE.md#limits), and the way to report a vulnerability is in [SECURITY.md](SECURITY.md).
 
